A pool destroy takes its Irqs but leaves them in the line table.
The next interrupt or bind on the line would find memory that is no longer an Irq;
the line table records exactly the Irqs that are bound.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: line table names an irq that is gone

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -509,7 +509,6 @@ bool sched_forget(struct obj_header *o, bool preempt)
     }
     case CAP_IRQ:
         /* It was disarmed and its line masked as its notification was cleared; the line is free again. */
-        line_irq[((struct irq *)o)->line] = 0;
         break;
     default:
         break;
